    <string name="guard_router_router_help_country_source">When enabled, local traffic bypasses VPN. For example, if the router is in RU, RU sites and services use the router’s IP address. Traffic to foreign services uses the active VPN connection.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_home">The app automatically disconnects the phone’s current VPN connection when you join your trusted Wi-Fi network and pair with the router. When you leave that network, the app restores the phone’s previous connection using the last selected VPN profile.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_install_server">Enable this if your devices will connect to this router over VPN using its direct IP address. A separate server package will be installed and needs additional memory. Access can be configured after installation.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_open">Help: %1$s</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_password">Enter the OpenWrt administrator password. The username is usually root.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_pin">Set a six-digit PIN at the end of initial setup. Use it to pair with the configured router. Later, the PIN can only be changed in LuCI using the owner account. There is no preset PIN.\n\nPairing: up to 10 mobile devices per router; up to 10 routers in one app.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_profile">Choose a VPN profile from the phone to synchronize with the router. You can add it later.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_protocols">Choose which VPN protocols the router will support. Hysteria2 is selected by default. Other protocols can be added after pairing with the router.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_public_ip">If your router supports a static public IP address, it can act as a VPN gateway for your devices. Route: device → router; local traffic goes directly, while foreign traffic uses the active VPN connection.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_reset_foxhole">Delete only FoxHole settings, its PIN and client records. FoxHole will need to be configured again. OpenWrt and other application settings are preserved.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_setup_pair">Install adds the FoxHole package to a supported OpenWrt router. Connect pairs the phone with an already installed FoxHole package. OpenWrt firmware is neither installed nor updated.\n\nPairing: up to 10 mobile devices per router; up to 10 routers in one app.</string>
